<div id="2026-11-07-branch-hermes-launch" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-07 — Branch Hermes launch no longer waits on :9119 or the web process</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> The Git page Hermes button starts a branch dashboard with <code>hermes dashboard --isolated</code> and returns as soon as the process is spawned. The startup lock is non-blocking. A timestamped command line is written to <code>/tmp/hermes-dash-&lt;branch&gt;.log</code> before the spawn. A launcher error is shown in the dev console instead of leaving it at "(waiting for output…)".</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> :3001 is one Twiggy process. A blocking flock, or a 20-second wait for the dashboard port, froze that process, so the log poll never ran and the console looked stuck. <code>--isolated</code> was already the flag that keeps the launch off the fleet dashboard; the hang was in Comserv, not a missing host on :9119.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Util/BranchServerControl.pm</code>, <code>Comserv/root/static/js/git-dashboard.js</code>, <code>Comserv/root/static/css/git-dashboard.css</code>, <code>Comserv/t/branch_server_control.t</code>.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Verified 2026-11-09.</strong> Unit tests pass (<code>t/branch_server_control.t</code>, 30). <code>perl -c</code> and <code>node --check</code> clean. The launcher was exercised for real from the running :3001 instance: <code>open_or_start_hermes('3d', 4003)</code> returned in 0.00 s with <code>ok=1 started=1</code>, <code>/tmp/hermes-dash-3d.log</code> opened with the <code>hermes start</code> line, the dashboard printed <code>HERMES_DASHBOARD_READY port=9103</code> and served HTTP 302 on :9103 while :9119 stayed up on its original pid. That test dashboard was stopped afterwards.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Still owed.</strong> The browser click on <code>/admin/git</code>: hard-refresh, then Hermes on a branch with :9119 stopped, and confirm the console streams the boot log. Non-session requests to <code>/admin/branch_server_action</code> answer 302, so this check needs a logged-in session. Changes are uncommitted.</p>
</div>
